From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:14:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 61/61] LOCAL DEBUG: zink: ZINK_MEM_REPORT=<seconds> prints the
 screen's VkDeviceMemory

Debug aid for amazon-sheldonp's memory accounting; never sent.
ZINK_DEBUG=mem only prints its per-resource table when an allocation
fails, and it counts resources, not the memory behind them. With
ZINK_MEM_REPORT=N the screen counts its live VkDeviceMemory, how much of
it backs slabs, how much the slab entries in use take, and reads how much
sits idle in the BO cache, and prints one line to stderr at most every N
seconds from end-of-frame flushes; with ZINK_DEBUG=mem also the table.
Off by default (no counting).

Generated-by: LLM
